        "original_id": "88e999b2-bef6-51b4-9789-43ff03d7f7a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lysichiton, Ageratum, Orontioideae, Orontium, Symplocarpus\n- Taxonomy: Araceae, Asteraceae, Eupatorieae, genera, subfamily\n\nFacts:\n- Lysichiton is a plant genus in the family Araceae.\n- Ageratum, also called whiteweed in the USA, is a plant genus of 40 to 60 tropical and warm temperate flowering annual and perennial species in the family Asteraceae and the tribe Eupatorieae.\n- Orontioideae is a subfamily consisting of three genera: Lysichiton, Orontium, and Symplocarpus.\n- Lysichiton includes one to two species of skunk cabbage from North America and Asia.\n- Orontium, known as golden club, has one living species from eastern North America and two extinct species known from fossils.\n- Symplocarpus includes several species of skunk cabbage from North America and Asia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
